The composite out connector was NTSC and wasn't supposed to work at any
higher resolutions. DOS had a "mode bw80" command which instructed the
graphics card to output just the luminance so you could display 640x200
on monochrome monitors and B&W TVs without blurring.

CGA monitors with a DB-9 connector were TTL, with each colour (including
the intensity bit) and sync signals on separate pins, so they could do
640x200 in colour with no problems.

